  "articleBody": "It's a really smart question to ask if your website is truly equipped for the AI search landscape. Many businesses assume if their site looks good and ranks well traditionally, they're set for AI Overviews. But AI systems have some unique preferences that might surprise you! It's not about complex \"AI markup\" or a separate AI-only version of your site; it's about fundamental web health and structured clarity.\n\nOne of the first things AI systems look at is **crawlability and indexability**. Can AI bots even access and understand your content? Issues with `robots.txt` files, heavy JavaScript, or content hidden within images can make your site practically invisible to AI. Your content needs to be available as plain, accessible text.\n\nNext, consider your **website's speed and mobile experience**. AI systems, and users, prefer fast-loading, mobile-friendly sites. Core Web Vitals aren't just for human users; they're signals of a well-maintained, accessible site that AI appreciates. Slow load times or a clunky mobile interface can definitely hinder your AI visibility.\n\nThen there's the crucial aspect of **structured data**. AI thrives on clearly organized information. Properly implemented JSON-LD schema (like `FAQPage` or `LocalBusiness`) tells AI exactly what your content means and how it relates to your services. But be careful – inaccurate or mismatched schema can be worse than none at all.\n\nFinally, think about **content clarity and direct answers**. AI Overviews are designed to provide direct answers to questions. If your website buries key information, is overly verbose, or doesn't directly address common queries, AI will struggle to cite you. It needs explicit answers that can be easily extracted.\n\nHow to Audit Your Website for AI Search Readiness:\n\nStart by checking your Google Search Console for any crawl errors or indexation issues. Use tools to test your site's mobile-friendliness and loading speed. Validate your structured data using Google's Rich Results Test. Most importantly, look at your content through the lens of a question-answering machine: does it provide clear, concise answers to the questions your customers are asking? If you have a large, complex site, or are struggling with technical issues, a professional technical SEO specialist or agency can provide invaluable help.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-23"
